## Chapter 9: Failure Modes and Emergency Protocols

**BCI signal loss** → $\rho$ forced to 0; copilot holds jogging pace (3 m/s) and announces "autonomy engaged."

**Single exo-leg actuator failure** → asymmetric gait recovery protocol: copilot compensates contralateral leg stiffness to maintain balance; speed reduced by 40%.

**Power loss** → passive spring lockout engages; exo-legs become rigid stilt extensions for controlled deceleration; user decelerates to walking in < 3 strides.

**CBF infeasibility (extreme perturbation)** → emergency stop command: all actuators generate maximum braking torque bilaterally; harness tether engages.

**User incapacitation** → gyroscopic IMU detects loss of postural control; copilot initiates controlled sit-down manoeuvre via hip-joint servo-braking.

