## Appendix D — Optimal User-Controlled Subspace

The user's four controlled parameters are chosen via the GSVD of $(\mathbf{J}_{\mathrm{loc}}, \mathbf{J}_{\mathrm{bal}})$:

$$\mathbf{J}_{\mathrm{loc}} = \mathbf{U}\boldsymbol{\Sigma}_l\mathbf{R},\quad \mathbf{J}_{\mathrm{bal}} = \mathbf{V}\boldsymbol{\Sigma}_b\mathbf{R},$$

with $\mathbf{R}$ invertible ($8 \times 8$). Generalized singular values $\sigma_i = \sigma_{l,i}/\sigma_{b,i}$ rank the stride modulation directions by speed authority per unit balance disturbance. The optimal subspace $S^*$ is spanned by the four columns of $\mathbf{R}^{-1}$ with the largest $\sigma_i$ satisfying $\sigma_{b,i} \le \delta$. This guarantees maximum locomotor effect per unit of ZMP deviation — the safest fast directions in stride space.

