## Appendix F — Control Barrier Function Construction

**F.1 ZMP-based safe set.** The ZMP in the sagittal plane is:

$$p_{\mathrm{ZMP}} = \frac{\sum_i F_{z,i} x_i + \sum_i \dot{L}_{y,i}}{\sum_i F_{z,i}},$$

where $F_{z,i}$ are vertical ground reaction forces at contact point $i$. The safe set imposes $|p_{\mathrm{ZMP}} - p_{\mathrm{support}}| \le \delta_{\mathrm{poly}}$. Taking $h(\mathbf{x}) = \delta_{\mathrm{poly}}^2 - (p_{\mathrm{ZMP}} - p_{\mathrm{support}})^2$, the Lie derivatives are computed analytically from the SLIP model linearisation.

**F.2 Robust tightening.** For frame compliance $\epsilon$, the tightened constraint:

$$h^{\mathrm{rob}}(\mathbf{x}) = \delta_{\mathrm{poly}}^2 - (\mathbf{J}_{\mathrm{bal}}\dot{\mathbf{q}}_g)^2 - \epsilon\|\dot{\mathbf{q}}_g\|(2\delta_{\mathrm{poly}} + \epsilon\|\dot{\mathbf{q}}_g\|) \ge 0$$

guarantees true balance safety under any $\Delta\mathbf{J}_{\mathrm{bal}}$ of norm $\le \epsilon$.

