**H.1 MVE — VR treadmill.** 12 participants; 20 sessions; two-class motor imagery (left-hand vs. right-hand). 64-channel EEG, 512 Hz, Riemannian MDM classifier. VR shows spring-leg avatar. ITR estimated online via Wolpaw formula. Statistical test: mixed-effects model of gait bifurcation rate vs. ITR; expected negative exponential. Falsification: if bifurcation rate < 0.5/min for ITR < 60 bits/min, H1 is falsified.

**H.2 Physical prototype.** Bilateral spring-leg exoskeleton, 4 kg/leg, instrumented treadmill (Kistler force plate), safety harness. Sinusoidal stride frequency sweeps identify $\tau_{\mathrm{tend}}$, $k_{\mathrm{eff}}$ vs. $k_{\mathrm{cmd}}$ relationships via least-squares fit.

**H.3 Shared autonomy benchmark.** Full autonomy vs. 4-parameter BCI vs. attempted 8-DOF direct control. Dual-task paradigm (auditory n-back) to vary cognitive load. Trust factor $\rho(t)$ logged at 100 Hz. Metrics: top speed, CBF interventions/min, VO₂ (metabolic cost), NASA-TLX workload.

